          "body": "The opening weekend of the PREM Rugby season saw a significant Welsh influence, with several high-profile exports making immediate impressions across the league. Gloucester captain Dewi Lake marked his debut with two tries and a player-of-the-match award, while Aaron Wainwright delivered a standout performance for Leicester Tigers. Saracens scrum-half Tomos Williams also earned acclaim, with head coach Joe Shaw noting, \"Considering he's just come to a new team and had to learn everything very quickly, it just shows what his class is.\""
