          "heading": "Australia and South Africa confirm landmark 100th Test match meeting",
          "body": "Rugby Australia has confirmed the international calendar for 2027, which includes a historic 100th Test match against the Springboks. The rivalry, dating back to 1933, will be renewed twice during the year, with the second encounter set to mark the centenary milestone. This announcement follows the Wallabies' recent 42-38 victory over the world champions in Perth, a match that saw the hosts hold off a late comeback despite being reduced to 11 men during a chaotic final quarter."
